WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.618 --> 00:00:21.001
arrived as the rebels were debating which of the five men should get the four uniforms.

2
00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:25.384
"Someone can have my uniform," Valjean volunteered.

3
00:00:25.404 --> 00:00:27.005
"Who is that man?"

4
00:00:27.605 --> 00:00:28.466
asked Courfeyrac.

5
00:00:28.886 --> 00:00:29.867
"How did he get in here?"

6
00:00:29.887 --> 00:00:32.380
"I know him," said Marius.

7
00:00:32.941 --> 00:00:34.141
"His name is Fauchelevent."

8
00:00:34.821 --> 00:00:38.223
Marius' response told the men that Valjean was on their side.

9
00:00:38.243 --> 00:00:41.424
"The guard let me pass," said Valjean.

10
00:00:41.444 --> 00:00:45.206
"He must have thought that just one National Guard was not a threat."

11
00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:48.688
"Welcome, fellow citizen," said Enjolras.

12
00:00:48.708 --> 00:00:55.351
"Your actions will save one man's life, but do you realize we're all going to die in here?"

13
00:00:56.311 --> 00:01:01.986
Valjean did not respond; he was busy exchanging clothes with the man who would wear his uniform.

14
00:01:02.946 --> 00:01:07.188
It was rapidly growing light as the rebels prepared for the attack on their barricade.

15
00:01:08.428 --> 00:01:10.009
They did not have long to wait.

16
00:01:11.029 --> 00:01:14.071
Soon a huge cannon appeared at the end of the street.

17
00:01:14.831 --> 00:01:17.372
Smoke rose from the cannon as the fuse was lit.

18
00:01:18.292 --> 00:01:20.093
"Fire!" ordered Enjolras.

19
00:01:20.593 --> 00:01:22.374
The rebel gunners fired at the cannon.

20
00:01:22.894 --> 00:01:26.856
The air filled with thick smoke and a terrible explosion from the cannon.

21
00:01:27.788 --> 00:01:32.950
When the smoke cleared, the rebels saw that not a single man in the barricade was hurt.

22
00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:34.950
"Bravo for the gunners!"

23
00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:36.451
shouted Courfeyrac.

24
00:01:37.371 --> 00:01:39.632
The big cannon fired at the barricade again.

25
00:01:40.272 --> 00:01:43.413
At the same moment, Gavroche tumbled into the barricade.

26
00:01:43.933 --> 00:01:46.674
His appearance there caused more shock than the cannon did.

27
00:01:46.694 --> 00:01:48.594
"What are you doing here?"

28
00:01:48.954 --> 00:01:49.715
cried Marius.

29
00:01:49.735 --> 00:01:51.435
"Who told you to come back?

30
00:01:52.015 --> 00:01:53.856
Did you put my letter in Cosette's hands?"

31
00:01:54.836 --> 00:01:57.597
Gavroche knew that he would be in trouble if he told the truth.

32
00:01:59.237 --> 00:02:01.478
"She was sleeping, so I left it with the porter.

33
00:02:02.158 --> 00:02:03.478
She'll get it when she wakes up."

34
00:02:04.459 --> 00:02:07.820
Meanwhile Enjolras was dealing with a hole in the barricade.

35
00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:11.441
"We need a mattress to deaden the effect of the cannon."

36
00:02:12.201 --> 00:02:13.921
"Look up there," said Courfeyrac.

37
00:02:14.541 --> 00:02:18.222
Someone had hung a mattress in front of his windows to keep them from breaking.

38
00:02:18.242 --> 00:02:20.683
"But how will we get the mattress down?"

39
00:02:21.603 --> 00:02:27.354
Valjean had been sitting in a corner, but now he sprang to his feet and took careful aim

40
00:02:27.394 --> 00:02:28.094
at the mattress.

41
00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:32.137
With two shots, he cut the ropes that held it.

42
00:02:32.617 --> 00:02:35.378
The mattress fell to the street outside the barricade.

43
00:02:36.299 --> 00:02:42.602
Without waiting for instructions, he clambered over the top of the barricade, seized the mattress, and brought it

44
00:02:42.642 --> 00:02:43.423
back inside.

45
00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:48.926
A cheer went up from the rebels, and Enjolras rushed to shake Valjean's hand.

46
00:02:48.946 --> 00:02:52.348
"You're a hero of the republic!"

47
00:02:52.796 --> 00:02:54.037
exclaimed Enjolras.

48
00:02:54.997 --> 00:02:56.878
The assault on the barricade continued.

49
00:02:57.519 --> 00:03:03.122
The attackers hoped that those inside would soon run out of ammunition, and indeed that was happening.

50
00:03:04.142 --> 00:03:09.165
Marius suddenly spotted someone outside the barricade gathering bullets from dead soldiers.

51
00:03:09.805 --> 00:03:15.509
It was Gavroche, who had taken a basket from the tavern and was quietly going about this task.

52
00:03:16.449 --> 00:03:18.490
"Gavroche! What are you doing out there?"

53
00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:19.931
exclaimed Marius.

54
00:03:19.951 --> 00:03:21.312
"You'll be killed!"

55
00:03:22.436 --> 00:03:23.697
"Stop calling to him!"

56
00:03:24.077 --> 00:03:24.957
hissed Courfeyrac.

57
00:03:24.977 --> 00:03:27.278
"You're only drawing attention to him."

58
00:03:28.258 --> 00:03:33.120
They watched in horror and fascination as Gavroche danced around the incoming bullets.

59
00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:36.342
"It's raining hard out here this morning!"

60
00:03:36.742 --> 00:03:38.382
Gavroche teased the attackers.

61
00:03:38.403 --> 00:03:40.503
"You'll have to do better than that!

62
00:03:40.944 --> 00:03:45.865
You'll never hit—" At that moment Gavroche was struck by a bullet.

63
00:03:46.546 --> 00:03:49.787
Marius sprang out of the barricade with Courfeyrac on his heels.

64
00:03:50.827 --> 00:03:53.861
But it was too late; Gavroche had been killed.

65
00:03:54.541 --> 00:03:59.343
Courfeyrac brought back the basket of ammunition while Marius carried Gavroche's body.

66
00:04:00.143 --> 00:04:03.845
A bullet grazed Marius' forehead, but he hardly noticed.

67
00:04:03.865 --> 00:04:06.866
"Poor Gavroche," thought Marius.

68
00:04:07.646 --> 00:04:09.587
"His father saved my father's life.

69
00:04:10.588 --> 00:04:12.669
If only I'd been able to do the same for him."

70
00:04:13.869 --> 00:04:17.871
Back inside, the rebels feverishly worked to build up the barricade.

71
00:04:17.891 --> 00:04:20.672
"Get this spy out of the way!"

72
00:04:21.308 --> 00:04:24.691
Enjolras pointed at Javert, who was still tied to a post.

73
00:04:24.711 --> 00:04:27.333
"The last man alive should kill him."

74
00:04:28.174 --> 00:04:29.876
"Excuse me," said Valjean.

75
00:04:29.896 --> 00:04:32.218
"You called me a hero earlier.

76
00:04:32.818 --> 00:04:35.421
Might I have the honor of killing the spy now?"

77
00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:36.922
"Go ahead!"

78
00:04:37.723 --> 00:04:42.166
Someone was cleaning Marius' wound when Valjean untied Javert from the post.

79
00:04:43.748 --> 00:04:48.192
As Valjean led the prisoner away, Marius suddenly recognized him.

80
00:04:49.196 --> 00:04:51.337
"That's the policeman who gave me the pistol!

81
00:04:52.077 --> 00:04:52.957
He's a spy?"

82
00:04:53.857 --> 00:04:59.299
While Marius was pondering this, Valjean took Javert to an alleyway leading out of the barricade.

83
00:04:59.939 --> 00:05:01.900
Neither man said a word to the other.

84
00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:05.581
Valjean stopped and looked Javert in the eye.

85
00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:08.661
"Do you recognize me now?"

86
00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:09.942
asked Valjean.

87
00:05:09.962 --> 00:05:11.302
"Of course."

88
00:05:11.802 --> 00:05:13.523
Javert gave a rueful smile.

89
00:05:13.543 --> 00:05:17.504
"I suppose it's appropriate that my life should end this way."

90
00:05:18.556 --> 00:05:21.598
Valjean took a knife and cut the last of Javert's bonds.

91
00:05:21.618 --> 00:05:23.359
"You're free to go."

92
00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:29.422
Javert was not easily astonished, but he stood there speechless.

93
00:05:29.442 --> 00:05:34.145
"I don't expect to get out of here alive," Valjean continued.

94
00:05:34.165 --> 00:05:38.927
"But if I do, I want you to know where to find me.

95
00:05:39.568 --> 00:05:44.650
I go by the name Fauchelevent and live at 7 Rue de l'Homme Armé."

96
00:05:45.571 --> 00:05:47.332
Javert shook his head in disbelief.

97
00:05:48.044 --> 00:05:50.585
"This isn't the way that things are supposed to end.

98
00:05:51.205 --> 00:05:52.305
I'd rather you killed me."

99
00:05:52.325 --> 00:05:55.326
"Just get out of here before I change my mind!"

100
00:05:56.247 --> 00:05:57.887
Javert slowly walked away.

101
00:05:58.407 --> 00:06:01.668
When he was out of sight, Valjean fired a shot.

102
00:06:02.368 --> 00:06:03.489
Marius heard the shot.

103
00:06:03.509 --> 00:06:05.870
"Javert is dead," he thought.

104
00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:08.570
And now the serious battle began.

105
00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:13.532
A massive column of soldiers entered the street and began firing upon the barricade.

106
00:06:14.444 --> 00:06:19.108
They swarmed over the top of the barricade and fought with the students and workers.

107
00:06:19.789 --> 00:06:22.791
Courfeyrac was killed, and so were many others.

108
00:06:23.512 --> 00:06:24.993
Enjolras remained unhurt.

109
00:06:25.914 --> 00:06:28.836
Marius fought on, his head covered with wounds.

110
00:06:30.418 --> 00:06:34.341
Suddenly a bullet pierced his shoulder, and he felt himself falling.

111
00:06:34.361 --> 00:06:38.124
"I'll be taken prisoner now, and shot," he thought.

112
00:06:38.785 --> 00:06:41.868
As he passed out, his last thought was of Cosette.

113
00:06:43.076 --> 00:06:49.019
Seconds later Marius was indeed taken prisoner, but his captor was not a French soldier.

114
00:06:49.759 --> 00:06:54.321
Instead Valjean picked up Marius and carried him into a corner.

115
00:06:55.261 --> 00:06:58.823
There the older man stopped and let Marius slide to the ground.

116
00:06:59.543 --> 00:07:01.063
Their situation was grim.

117
00:07:01.944 --> 00:07:06.286
They would be safe for a few more minutes, but the battle raged all around them.

118
00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:08.967
They'd never escape this massacre.

119
00:07:09.867 --> 00:07:11.868
Valjean looked at the barricade in front of them.

120
00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:14.702
A row of soldiers' bayonets sat above it.

121
00:07:15.542 --> 00:07:19.785
The tavern was behind Valjean and Marius, but they could get trapped in there.

122
00:07:20.546 --> 00:07:23.988
Valjean stared at the street, hoping an answer would come to him.

123
00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:29.713
Then suddenly he saw it: a metal grate covering an opening in the street.

124
00:07:30.313 --> 00:07:35.897
Valjean pulled up the grate, loaded Marius onto his back, and lowered himself into the opening.

125
00:07:36.778 --> 00:07:39.840
Below, everything around them was completely dark.

126
00:07:40.952 --> 00:07:45.074
There was deep peace, absolute silence, night.

127
00:07:46.155 --> 00:07:50.938
It was not unlike the time Valjean had carried Cosette over the wall and into the convent.

128
00:07:51.558 --> 00:07:54.960
Above their heads, he could hear troops storming the tavern.

129
00:07:55.861 --> 00:07:58.902
At first Valjean could see nothing in the blackness.

130
00:07:59.563 --> 00:08:03.905
He reached out one hand and then the other to touch the walls around him.

131
00:08:04.866 --> 00:08:06.847
The ground below his feet was solid.

132
00:08:07.427 --> 00:08:08.148
Where were they?

133
00:08:08.924 --> 00:08:11.287
A foul smell gave Valjean the answer.

134
00:08:12.088 --> 00:08:16.494
For the moment they were safe in the sewers below the streets of Paris.

135
00:08:17.195 --> 00:08:18.556
But how would they get out?
